      {
        "position": 8,
        "title": "Well made, good support and priced competitively",
        "text": "I recently acquired new tenants who have two cute dogs in an upper level rental in my home and property. I always try my best to make them feel at home and usually give them something to welcome them.Knowing how much my tenants love their pet dogs I wanted to give them something practically and functional and when I saw this dog bed I thought it would be a nice gesture and also be something they could really use every day so I decided to order this.They have a small mixed breed and one black lab.The black lab is on the big side at just 2 years old and so I decided on the Extra Large size so perhaps both can lay and relax on this bed at the same time.While there are a vast amount of these types of beds available what caught my eye about this particular brand and bed was the benefit of the design it boasted on its ad.I could see how this bed due to its fillings and layers inside would be so much better for the fridge and help them to maintain a healthy position when laying down or sleeping.Of course they were extremely appreciative and I made it a point to ask the tenants for feedback for the purposes of this review.They did comment that the dogs truly enjoy this bed and had no problem warming up and using it right away. They seem very comfortable and that it supports them quite well with good layersA removable and washable cover always helps but this has an additional anti-slip feature at the bottom which they mentioned was great because the bed is not moving around so much at all like some others they have had in the past!So, overall this is an excellent dog bed and is seeing the fruits of labor in the design and material with the dogs loving the comfort. Knowing it’s providing good support allows me to feel good about the choice and justify the cost easily.",
        "rating": 5,
